From: SM-G955N Ubuntu port contributors
Subject: [PATCH] fbdev: DECON: retain an active native framebuffer console

The Android close path unconditionally disables the display. Native probes
close their fd while fbcon still owns the framebuffer, blanking the panel.
Keep the panel for that console owner; explicit blank/shutdown is unchanged.

diff --git a/drivers/video/fbdev/exynos/dpu/decon_core.c b/drivers/video/fbdev/exynos/dpu/decon_core.c
--- a/drivers/video/fbdev/exynos/dpu/decon_core.c
+++ b/drivers/video/fbdev/exynos/dpu/decon_core.c
@@ -3320,6 +3320,13 @@ int decon_release(struct fb_info *info, int user)
 	struct decon_win *win = info->par;
 	struct decon_device *decon = win->decon;
 
+	/* A native framebuffer console is another display owner. Closing a
+	 * userspace probe must not turn off its active panel. Explicit blank
+	 * and device shutdown still perform the normal power transitions.
+	 */
+	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_FRAMEBUFFER_CONSOLE) && info->fbcon_par)
+		return 0;
+
 	decon_info("%s + : %d\n", __func__, decon->id);
 
 	if (decon->id && decon->dt.out_type == DECON_OUT_DSI) {
